WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.916
A pole can look sound while hiding deterioration.

00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:07.873
Appearance is only part of inspection.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:13.403
These outside and cut-face images are model views, not field evidence.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.691
A pre-climb assessment must consider more.

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:21.264
This transparent model exposes entered decay.

00:00:23.006 --> 00:00:25.751
The section shows its position and remaining wood.

00:00:26.688 --> 00:00:31.185
Ultrasound contributes evidence in practice, requiring reliable measurements

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:32.911
and validated interpretation.

00:00:33.849 --> 00:00:37.300
This geometry is prescribed, not measured acoustically.

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:43.163
The red arrow represents a simple sideways tip load.

00:00:44.905 --> 00:00:48.533
It does not depict a climber or all the forces from their equipment.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:53.873
A real assessment must include actual work loads, the planned procedure

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:55.163
and ground conditions.

00:00:56.833 --> 00:01:00.149
Inspection evidence supports an approved work procedure.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.178
This repeating ultrasound view is a teaching simulation.

00:01:06.116 --> 00:01:10.015
The laboratory has no validated climb decision rules and cannot give

00:01:10.029 --> 00:01:10.668
clearance.

00:01:11.605 --> 00:01:14.662
Follow the complete inspection and escalation process.
